Z||000000||isthiswhereiputausername?||08-17-2001||02:44 PM||||After a complete restore of my interior, the only thing that looks out of place is DIRTY seatbelts.  anyone have a quick cure for cleaning them?(dust,little grease,etc) would a steam cleaner do it? or does anyone have a better idea?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>thanks<P><BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||08-17-2001||02:54 PM||||I would think some warm soapy water maybe some goop hand cleaner and rinseing with clean water I dont think Iwould use a brush as this will cause the fabric to fray  and look worn out hope this helps||||reg||1
Z||000002||Max The Chainsaw||08-17-2001||03:49 PM||||I took mine out and took them to work where we have a steam cleaner. Pulled em out all the way , laid em on the floor and steamed away.<P>Looked like new when I was done.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||08-17-2001||07:30 PM||||Laundry soap, simple green, citrisolv, anything like that ususally works. Simple green and citrisolv rinse out pretty easy. Avoid harsh stuff and solvents.||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||08-18-2001||01:13 AM||||I pulled mine out all the way and sprayed foam carpet cleaner on them, brushed it, then wiped with cloth. left em pulled out to dry.||||reg||1
